cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the results it reproduces, please cite both the
  software and the accompanying manuscript.
title: >-
  A Practical Evaluation of Knowledge Preservation and Adaptation to Outlier
  NIST Writers in Federated Learning
abstract: >-
  Code and records of a practical evaluation of adapting a deployed handwriting
  model to the outlier NIST SD19 writers it serves worst through federated
  learning, while preserving what it knows of the writers it was trained on:
  communication scheduling, aggregation forms and client-side regularisation.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/keshtkarsadegh/fl-outlier-writers-nist"
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - catastrophic forgetting
  - knowledge distillation
  - client heterogeneity
  - reproducibility
